===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*steh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|stonden}}, {{m|enm|standen|pos=verb}} and {{m|enm|stand}}, {{m|enm|stond|pos=noun, from the verb}}, from {{inh|en|ang|standan||to stand, occupy a place}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*standan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*standaną||to stand}}, from Pre-Germanic {{m|ine-pro|*sth₂-n-t-´}}, an innovative extended ''n''-infixed form of {{der|en|ine-pro|*steh₂-}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|stand||to stand}}, {{cog|stq|stounde||to stand}}, {{cog|fy|stean||to stand}}, dialectal {{cog|de|standen||to stand}}, {{cog|da|stande||to stand}}, {{cog|sv|stånda||to stand}}, {{cog|no|standa||to stand}}, {{cog|fo|standa||to stand}}, {{cog|is|standa||to stand}}, {{cog|got|𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌽𐌳𐌰𐌽}}, {{cog|ru|стоя́ть||to stand}}. Also from {{m|ine-pro|*steh₂-}}: {{cog|ga|seas}}, {{cog|la|stare}}, {{cog|lt|stóti}}, {{cog|cu|стояти}}, {{cog|sq|shtoj||to increase}}, {{cog|grc|ἵστημι||to put}}, {{cog|ae|𐬵𐬌𐬱𐬙𐬀𐬌𐬙𐬌}}, {{cog|sa|तिष्ठति}}. From the related {{cog|gem-pro|*stāną||to stand}}: {{cog|fy|stean}}, {{cog|nl|staan}}, {{cog|de|stehen}}, {{cog|da|stå}}.
{{col-bottom}}

